    "scope": "Prove exactly the single second wreath-product Specht branching theorem6.1 over an arbitrary field, with every original multipartition/base-Specht indexing and dominance-ordered quotient convention intact. Complete new nonredundant double-coset system, conjugated tensor action and exact-functor filtration proof retained. No first branching theorem4.1 or component/multiplicity variation counted.",
    "prerequisites": "Classical Mackey theory, ordinary symmetric-group Specht branching (James Theorem9.3), tensor/induction identities and the explicitly cited Young-subgroup tableau double-coset correspondence are ordinary prerequisites. All selected new representatives, stabilizer computation, tensor action and transported filtrations are fully authored here. Source Proposition3.1 omits a proof for a different first-branching result, which remains uncounted context and is not a premise of the selected second proof.",
    "literal_source_interfaces": "One unselected illustrative semistandard skew-tableau display and its example text at native189--197 are omitted; exact tableau/skew/semistandard definitions remain. Two isolated pointers to that example in185/188 are removed by an inventoried finite prose-only adaptation. The genuine original TikZ mytab macro and every retained proof/tableau diagram are preserved; it is author-written native code, not an emulation of ytableau. No denied package acquisition or mathematical repair.",
    "difficulty_level": "H1",
    "difficulty_reason": "The proof constructs an explicit nonredundant Mackey double-coset system for the wreath subgroup pair, computes the conjugated stabilizer action on tensor factors, and transports the ordinary dominance-ordered Specht filtration through exact functors. Once ordinary Mackey theory and symmetric-group branching are granted, those coupled modular constructions remain substantive obligations beyond standard qualification exercises. The unselected first branching rule and numerical multiplicity specializations add no count.",
